("v11098", "scalar", "Skip to the story\nA\nAaron Alderman\nThe mission\nThoughts\nMy Mind\n\nAARON ALDERMAN / A PERSONAL EXPEDITION\n\nInside the mind of a\nmodern-day\nsourcerer.\nANOTHER SIDE\n\nPhysics, faith, machines, and the work of remembering care.\n\nLink to this world ↗\n\nBEGIN WITH\n\nQuestions\n\nHow do I build software that earns trust?\n\n↗\nThreads\n\nFollow understanding, permission and repair.\n\n↗\nAtlas / Map\n\nFind evidence, boundaries and ways to repair.\n\n↗\nThere’s more beneath the surface.\nExplore the systems, applications and tools\n↓\n\nTHE WORK THROUGH A SOURCERER’S EYES\n\nHow an idea becomes something people can inspect, use and change.\n\nSee all projects ↓\n\nFOUNDATION & PLATFORM\n\nMake the rules visible.\n\nTemple and Sourcery form the execution foundation and authoring platform beneath this ecosystem. I want power, permission and change to have an account people can inspect.\n\nExecution\nFoundation\n\nTemple\n\nAccountable execution. Explicit rules, checked changes and a history you can inspect.\n\nI want execution and change to remain inspectable.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nPlatform\nBuilt on Temple\n\nSourcery\n\nAuthor meaning and compose systems, built on Temple.\n\nA shared process algebra for composing meaning and behaviour.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nAPPLICATIONS & PROGRAMMES\n\nPut an explanation to the test.\n\nKnowledge and scientific inquiry need more than a convincing answer: sources, disagreement and checks another person can repeat.\n\nKnowledge\nApplication\n\nClaimipedia\n\nClaims, evidence and disagreement, with their sources and history still attached.\n\nKeep an answer connected to its evidence and its objections.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nResearch\nScience & research\n\nClaimipedia Science\n\nScientific inquiry with explicit models, evidence and reproducible checks.\n\nA concrete scientific programme with explicit models and reproducible checks.\n\nFirst use case: Relational Geometry Programme\n\nAgent-assisted research with Mission Control →\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nTAKING SHAPE\n\nBuild the next possibility.\n\nThese projects are in development. Each explores a different setting for the same question: what should a system make possible, and how can people remain in charge?\n\nCreation\nIn progress\n\nWorldwright\n\nCompose stories with more than one way through.\n\nExplore how story choices can compose into a continuing world.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nCoordination\nIn progress\n\nKingdom\n\nFaith, formation and the shape of shared life.\n\nExplore the structures of formation and shared life.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nSimulation\nIn progress\n\nSimulation\n\nExplore how systems behave, from models of possible worlds to an industrial chain from mine to port.\n\nMake mechanisms and their possible consequences explicit.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\nWorld Modelling\nFoundry\n\nPractice\nIn progress\n\nTradie\n\nConnect enquiries, commitments and work.\n\nFollow a commitment from enquiry into actual work.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nCoordination\nLocal prototype\n\nUsewords\n\nStart with what matters. Develop questions, positions and proposals with AI assistance, while keeping people’s words, uncertainty and disagreement visible.\n\nGive what matters a structure people can question, develop and change.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nCreation\nIn progress\n\nCreator Studio\n\nShape an idea as a story, a film or an interactive experience.\n\nBring several creative forms into one developing workspace.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nTOOLS & WORKBENCHES\n\nGive the work a next step.\n\nSmaller tools for research, coordination and practice. Their stated maturity still matters; a working example and a complete product are different stages.\n\nCreation\nLive example\n\nEncounter\n\nInspect meaning. Follow a change.\n\nThe Encounter language and studio for inspecting meaning and following change.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nCoordination\nAgent harness\n\nMission Control\n\nSourcery’s agent harness and automatic workflow mechanism.\n\nCoordinate agent-assisted research without hiding the work behind it.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nSimulation\nEncounter prototype\n\nThe Field\n\nPractise attention, choice and responsibility through an encounter and its possible consequences.\n\nA framework for modelling how choices change relationships and what people can do next.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nPractice\nTooling\n\nSuperCRM\n\nPeople, obligations and coordinated work.\n\nKeep people and obligations visible alongside coordinated work.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nPractice\nTooling\n\nTimesheet\n\nTime, approval and a traceable record.\n\nGive time and approval a traceable account.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nCoordination\nTooling\n\nWorkgarden\n\nGive work a place and a next step.\n\nTurn an unfinished task into a place and a next step.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nCoordination\nTooling\n\nHarborboard\n\nPlan work. See what depends on what.\n\nSee dependencies before changing a plan.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\n\nCare\nSource: Relationship Navigator\n\nRelationship Manager\n\nMake room for boundaries and repair.\n\nKeep boundaries and repair in view when assistance becomes complicated.\n\nExplore\n↗\nInspect\nAll projects · the complete catalogue\n\nCurrent theme: sourcerer.\n\nAaron Alderman\n\nA few things I’ve built. A few things I’m still trying to understand.\n\nGitHub ↗\nLinkedIn ↗\nBuilt with Worldwright.io ↗\nAssurance\nLicence ↗\nChristian stewardship covenant ↗")
